{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>To your gates.</b> According to the plain sense, this is the place of judgment, so that the claimant need not toil and chase after the defendant, but rather sit and watch for him — when will he pass by there? For he cannot avoid passing by way of the gate. And so we find: 'and Boaz went up to the gate and sat there, and behold, the redeemer was passing by, of whom Boaz had spoken.'" "<b>And you shall stone them with stones.</b> This is a model for 'in fire they shall burn him or her and them.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:08.196206886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}